# Teleport RELEASE policy verification RECOVERY root -- PUBLIC half.
#
# Dormant by design: the server signs with the primary root in normal operation
# and switches to this one only if the primary is compromised. Baked into every
# release build from the start because that direction is irreversible -- a client
# shipped without this key can never be taught to trust it later, so any release
# that omits it permanently loses its recovery path.
#
# What it does NOT do: it does not revoke the primary. A client trusts every root
# in its set equally, so removing a leaked primary still requires shipping a new
# client. Nor does switching to it happen by itself -- the server must re-endorse
# existing tenants, which is a deliberate, lossy operation. See the design spec
# 4.3 (D1) before assuming a rotation is seamless.
#
# PRIVATE half: generated in an offline ceremony and kept in offline cold storage.
# It must never touch an online system, and must not share custody with the
# primary root -- co-located roots fail together, which would make this second
# key pure overhead.
#
# SHA-256(DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo):
#   a45361da7f060b221458350e564d3bdc40683ae0256620e864e4326ef23a56a0
# Imported: 2026-08-10. Verify the fingerprint above against the ceremony record
# before trusting this file.
